escape from tarkov had their first alpha  livestream and we've seen a lot of  interest in this game from the shooter  community so here are five things that  we learned about the game number one  objectives as stated in the game's title  your goal is to escape from various  zones but we now know this will not only  involve scavenging but solving puzzles  finding secret rooms avoiding  environmental hazards such as minefields  and contending with both wave-based NPCs  called scavengers and other players in  private military factions such as bear  and you say players are free to engage  in gun fights with anyone but in the  alpha build too much player killing does  result in bad karma which can lead to  negative status effects such as becoming  sick the player controlled private  factions can have as many as ten to  fourteen players there will also be  non-combat NPC's in the game such as  traders number two bullet physics one of  the more interesting parts of the stream  was a demonstration of bullet physics  each bullet has velocity can penetrate  certain types of cover and has a chance  to ricochet ricochets happen when  bullets strike hard objects as they pass  through like cover and even when they  enter bodies it was mentioned that a  round can enter a player and exit in a  random Direction striking another player  the game also includes poorly  manufactured ammo types that can cause  weapons to jam or break checking to see  if a bullet is chambered was shown but  it's unclear if clearing weapon jams  will be a manual process one neat little  touch was how optics are modeled  realistically which should make them  slightly more difficult to use number  three gunfights the combat and escape  from tarkov as in many survival  scavenging games does come down to  finding and conserving ammo however most  of the gunfights we saw had relatively  long time to kill involving body shots  so gunfights should be fairly tense and  come down to lots of maneuvering players  start every life with a pistol and  deaths frequently found shotguns nearby  although a single bullet can kill a  player if they bleed out this was  quickly mitigated by health kits number  four there's a persistent unlock treat  there are five types of skills that a  player can use to build their character  give them an edge and make their post  death starts a little bit easier but  player skill will decline if they don't  play the game for long periods of time  additionally there's a mastering tree  where we saw an elite tier of skills  that did things like reduce the cost of  trading or greatly improve and control  and reduce recoil and number five the  heads-up display well in World escape  from tarkov has a very minimal heads-up  display in fact it's almost non-existent  players will have to click a button to  manually check how many bullets they  have left in the magazine however the  game also has a very intrusive inventory  screen at the time of this alpha any  weapon modding or inventory management  will make players completely vulnerable  as in similar games such as Daisy or  h1z1 my guess is you're going to be  killed very often while in the extensive  weapon modding menu so what do you think  of escape from tarkov so far does it  seem different enough from other  survival shooters to piqued your  interest leave your thoughts in the  comments below and if you saw this on  youtube and you want to see more likes  and subscribes are appreciated for more  coverage of escape from tarkov stay  tuned the game spot calm
 

